  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given the equation of tangent at vertex is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>and the focus is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/957085c2-8e98-4eb5-80fc-448d1775f7a2-image.png\" style=\"width: 199px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Now the perpendicular distance from focus to tangent is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Also given length of latus rectum<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>",
